## Context you should know, but not re-verify (out of scope for this snapshot)

`tests/test_verify.py` also changed in this commit — a fake's expected
content literal moved from `" "` to `"."`, because the underlying
`measure_frame` function now calls the (real, or here fake) API with `"."`
instead of `" "`. This is `BUG-001`
(`docs/bugs/BUG-001-espacio-en-blanco-rechazado-por-count-tokens.md` in this
checkout, if you want to read it — you don't need to, it's just background):
the real Anthropic API rejects whitespace-only content with a 400 error, and
was only discovered by Development running a real smoke test outside this
test suite (since this suite never touches the real network, by design).
That real-API verification is NOT something you can or should repeat here —
just confirm `tests/test_verify.py` still passes as part of the full suite
run above; that's the only claim being made about it in this scope.

